Question: What is the context length of `mistral-medium-3-5`?

Sources:
[1] https://docs.mistral.ai/models/mistral-medium-3-5-26-04
Mistral Medium 3.5 > Overview
Mistral Medium 3.5 > Overview

## Overview

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| API names | `mistral-medium-3-5`, `mistral-medium-3`, `mistral-medium-latest` |
| Slug | `mistral-medium-3-5-26-04` |
| Status | GA |
| Release date | 2026-04-28 |
| Version | 26.04 |
| Type | Open |
| Class | Generalist |
| Context length | 256k |
| Legacy | no |



[2] https://docs.mistral.ai/models/mistral-medium-3-5-26-04
Mistral Medium 3.5 > Weights
Mistral Medium 3.5 > Weights

## Weights

- Weights, 128B parameters, license Modified MIT, context 256k — [weights](https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Mistral-Medium-3.5-128B)



[3] https://docs.mistral.ai/resources/known-limitations#context-window
Known limitations > Context window
Known limitations > Context window

## Context window {#context-window}

| Model | Max context length |
|-------|-------------------|
| Mistral Large 3 | 256k tokens |
| Mistral Medium 3.5 | 256k tokens |
| Mistral Medium 3.1 | 128k tokens |
| Mistral Small 4 | 256k tokens |
| Codestral | 128k tokens |
| Devstral 2 | 256k tokens |
| Magistral Medium 1.2 | 128k tokens |
| Ministral 3 (3B / 8B / 14B) | 256k tokens |
| Mistral Nemo 12B | 128k tokens |

For the full and up-to-date list, see the [model cards](https://docs.mistral.ai/models).

- Requests exceeding the model's context window return a `400 Bad Request` error.
- Token counts include both input and output tokens. Plan your `max_tokens` accordingly.



[4] https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/audio/speech_to_text/offline_transcription#whats-the-maximum-audio-length
Offline > Offline Transcription > FAQ > What's the maximum audio length?
Offline > Offline Transcription > FAQ > What's the maximum audio length?

### What's the maximum audio length? {#whats-the-maximum-audio-length}

The maximum length will depend on the endpoint used, currently the limits are as follows:
- [Chat with Audio](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/audio/speech_to_text/offline_transcription#chat-with-audio): ≈20 minutes for [Voxtral Mini Transcribe](https://docs.mistral.ai/models/voxtral-mini-transcribe-25-07) and [Voxtral Small](https://docs.mistral.ai/models/voxtral-small-25-07).
- [Transcription](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/audio/speech_to_text/offline_transcription#transcription): ≈15 minutes for [Voxtral Mini Transcribe](https://docs.mistral.ai/models/voxtral-mini-transcribe-25-07) and [Voxtral Small](https://docs.mistral.ai/models/voxtral-small-25-07), and ≈3 hours for [Voxtral Mini Transcribe 2](https://docs.mistral.ai/models/voxtral-mini-transcribe-26-02).

> **Tip**
>
> Here are some tips if you need to handle longer audio files:
> - **Divide the audio into smaller segments:** Transcribe each segment individually. However, be aware that this might lead to a loss of context, difficulties in splitting the audio at natural pauses (such as mid-sentence), and the need to combine the transcriptions afterward.
> - **Increase the playback speed:** Send the file at a faster pace by speeding up the audio. Keep in mind that this can reduce audio quality and require adjusting the transcription timestamps to align with the original audio file.


[5] https://docs.mistral.ai/inference/model-lifecycle#naming-convention
Model lifecycle policy > Model naming convention
Model lifecycle policy > Model naming convention

## Model naming convention {#naming-convention}

Model identifiers use a `model-name-major-minor` format, for example `mistral-medium-3-5`.

General Availability models support three aliases:

| Alias | Example | Points to |
|---|---|---|
| `model-name-latest` | `mistral-medium-latest` | Latest General Availability version, across generations |
| `model-name-major` | `mistral-medium-3` | Latest minor version of that major generation |
| `model-name-major-minor` | `mistral-medium-3-5` | Fixed major and minor version |

Labs models are always prefixed with `labs-`. Public Preview models use the `major-minor` format but aren't eligible for a `-latest` or `-major` alias.

> **Warning**
>
> Aliases automatically switch to newer models once they reach General Availability. As a result, using an alias may expose you to silent updates in model behavior and pricing. For precise control, pin your deployment to a specific major.minor version identifier.



[6] https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/offline-models#hardware
Using offline models > Hardware
Using offline models > Hardware

## Hardware {#hardware}

For decent performance on long contexts, we recommend deploying at **FP8 precision** with a context length of around **128k**:

- **H100** or **A100** GPU for FP8 / 128k.
- **RTX 4090** or any **24 GB VRAM** GPU for 4-bit precision with a 32k context length.
- **CPU offload** also works on any machine with enough RAM, but it is significantly slower.

Adjust precision and context length based on the model and the hardware you have.

> **Note**
>
> The figures above are sized for Devstral Small 2 (24B dense). Mistral Small 4 (119B mixture-of-experts) needs significantly more VRAM to hold the weights: plan on at least one H100 80GB at FP8, more for long contexts.



[7] https://docs.mistral.ai/models/mistral-medium-3-25-05
