  "answer_markdown": "To configure **automatic user onboarding** and **passwordless sign-in** for a company in Mistral, the following applies based on the available plans and requirements:\n\n### **1. Automatic User Onboarding (via Email Domain Authentication)**\n- **Supported Plans**: **Team+** (Team plan and above) [4].\n- **Requirements**:\n  - A **verified domain** (domain verification is required for this feature) [4].\n  - Enabling **email-domain authentication** in **Administration › Settings** [2].\n  - Users with email addresses matching the verified domain (e.g., `@acme.com`) are **automatically added** to the organization without individual invitations [2].\n\n### **2. Passwordless Sign-In (via SAML SSO)**\n- **Supported Plans**: **Enterprise** (SAML SSO requires Enterprise) [1][5].\n- **Requirements**:\n  - A **verified domain** (domain verification is mandatory for SSO) [1][5].\n  - Configuration of **SAML SSO** with a corporate identity provider (e.g., Okta, Azure AD) [1][5].\n  - Users sign in **only with corporate credentials** (no separate Mistral password) [1][5].\n\n### **Key Notes**\n- Domain verification is **required for both features** but is available on **Team+ plans** (email-domain auth) and **Enterprise plans** (SAML SSO) [1][4][5].\n- **Email-domain authentication** allows automatic onboarding but **does not replace passwords** (users still need Mistral credentials unless combined with SSO) [2][4].\n- **SAML SSO** enables **true passwordless sign-in** but is **Enterprise-only** [1][5].",
