{
  "answer_markdown": "When creating a Skill from the editor in Mistral AI's Work, the **description** field is what Work reads at **discovery time** to decide whether to activate the Skill [2].\n\nThis field should be written as a **trigger condition**—specifying *when* to use the Skill, not just what it does. For example:\n- ❌ Vague: \"Helps with meetings.\"\n- ✅ Specific: \"Use when reviewing customer-call transcripts to extract objections and next steps.\" [2]\n\nThe description is critical because Work only loads the Skill's name and description (~100 tokens each) during discovery, and this text determines activation eligibility [1].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Work loads Skills through **progressive disclosure** in three stages: 1. **Discovery**: at session start, Work loads only each Skill's name and description (~100 tokens each), just enough to know when it might be relevant."
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "Fill in the form: ... **Description**: when Work should use this Skill. This text is what Work reads at discovery to decide whether to activate the Skill, so make it specific."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

