message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "Yes, when you start a remote coding session from a Slack thread with **Vibe Code Web**, the agent can open a **pull request (PR) for you to review** if the task involves a code change. This happens automatically after the agent completes its work in an isolated cloud sandbox, provided the context in the thread is clear and appropriate for a PR [1][2][3].\n\n### How to request a PR from Slack:\n1. Start a Slack thread with sufficient context (e.g., repository, issue description, or failing test).\n2. Mention the **Vibe Code app** with a request like:\n   ```text\n   @Vibe investigate the issue described in this thread and open a PR if there is a clear fix.\n   ```\n3. The agent will analyze the thread, create a Vibe Code Web session, and generate a **GitHub branch or PR** for review [2].\n\n### Key Notes:\n- The PR is created in GitHub, which remains the source of truth for review and merging [2].\n- Always review the PR in GitHub before merging, as AI-generated outputs may be inaccurate [4].\n- The feature is in **progressive rollout**, so availability may vary [2].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "The agent reads the thread context, works in an isolated cloud sandbox, and opens a GitHub pull request"
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "The coding agent can create a pull request for review."
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "@Vibe investigate the issue described in this thread and open a PR if there is a clear fix."
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "quote": "The result is a GitHub branch or pull request, when a code change is appropriate."
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "quote": "Outputs may be inaccurate — always review before merging."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

