message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "To call `POST /v1/audio/transcriptions` for **streaming transcription**, the following request body fields are **required** according to the documentation [2]:\n\n- `model` (string, required): The ID of the model to be used.\n\nFor supplying the audio file, you can use one of the following methods:\n\n### 1. **Direct File Upload (Recommended for Streaming)**\n   - Use the `file` field in `multipart/form-data` format.\n   - Example (cURL):\n     ```bash\n     curl --location 'https://api.mistral.ai/v1/audio/transcriptions' \\\n       --header \"x-api-key: $MISTRAL_API_KEY\" \\\n       --form 'file=@\"/path/to/your/file.mp3\"' \\\n       --form 'model=\"voxtral-mini-latest\"' \\\n       --form 'stream=true'\n     ```\n   - To specify a custom filename:\n     ```bash\n     file=@path/to/your/file.mp3;filename=custom_name.mp3\n     ```\n\n### 2. **Audio File URL**\n   - Use the `file_url` field to provide a URL to the audio file.\n   - Example (cURL):\n     ```bash\n     curl --location 'https://api.mistral.ai/v1/audio/transcriptions' \\\n       --header \"x-api-key: $MISTRAL_API_KEY\" \\\n       --form 'file_url=\"https://example.com/audio.mp3\"' \\\n       --form 'model=\"voxtral-mini-latest\"' \\\n       --form 'stream=true'\n     ```\n\n### 3. **Pre-uploaded File ID**\n   - Use the `file_id` field to reference a file previously uploaded via `/v1/files`.\n\n### Notes:\n- The `stream` field is optional but must be set to `true` if you explicitly want streaming behavior (though the endpoint `/v1/audio/transcriptions` with streaming defaults to SSE output when used correctly) [2].\n- Other optional fields like `language`, `diarize`, or `timestamp_granularities` can be included as needed.\n\nThe `file` field is the most common method for streaming transcription, as it allows direct upload of the audio file in the request body [2].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "The File object (not file name) to be uploaded. To upload a file and specify a custom file name you should format your request as such:"
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "file=@path/to/your/file.jsonl;filename=custom_name.jsonl"
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "Otherwise, you can just keep the original file name:"
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "file=@path/to/your/file.jsonl"
    },
    {
